From: crackerjacques <jack@supremeoverlordjabs.co>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: anbernic-td4310: use the timings that drive the RG Vita Pro panel

With the upstream mode (140.02MHz, 50/4/50 horizontal porches) the RG
Vita Pro panel shows every line shifted against the one above, so the
picture shears diagonally. 140.02MHz is not a rate the VOP can make
exactly, and the panel does not tolerate the difference.

Take the mode the Armbian RG Vita Pro image drives this panel with:
152MHz, 100/4/100 horizontal porches and a 5-line vsync, still 60Hz.
Feed DCLK_VP1, the video port the DSI hangs off, from VPLL at 1824MHz,
so the 152MHz pixel clock divides out exactly.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-anbernic-rg-vita-pro.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-anbernic-rg-vita-pro.dts
index 358dea4..a605209 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-anbernic-rg-vita-pro.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3576-anbernic-rg-vita-pro.dts
@@ -1192,6 +1192,9 @@
 };
 
 &vop {
+	assigned-clocks = <&cru PLL_VPLL>, <&cru DCLK_VP1_SRC>;
+	assigned-clock-parents = <0>, <&cru PLL_VPLL>;
+	assigned-clock-rates = <1824000000>, <0>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-anbernic-td4310.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-anbernic-td4310.c
index 3b6de1b..ee6d5ca 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-anbernic-td4310.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-anbernic-td4310.c
@@ -206,15 +206,15 @@ static int panel_anbernic_td4310_probe(struct mipi_dsi_device *dsi)
 }
 
 static const struct drm_display_mode anbernic_vitapro_mode = {
-	.clock = 140020,
+	.clock = 152000,
 	.hdisplay = 1080,
-	.hsync_start = 1080 + 50,
-	.hsync_end = 1080 + 50 + 4,
-	.htotal = 1080 + 50 + 4 + 50,
+	.hsync_start = 1080 + 100,
+	.hsync_end = 1080 + 100 + 4,
+	.htotal = 1080 + 100 + 4 + 100,
 	.vdisplay = 1920,
 	.vsync_start = 1920 + 15,
-	.vsync_end = 1920 + 15 + 4,
-	.vtotal = 1920 + 15 + 4 + 32,
+	.vsync_end = 1920 + 15 + 5,
+	.vtotal = 1920 + 15 + 5 + 32,
 	.flags = DRM_MODE_FLAG_NHSYNC | DRM_MODE_FLAG_NVSYNC,
 };
 
